{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1238409-changeling-2e-hedge-ghosts-and-twilight","id":1238409,"title":"Changeling 2e, Hedge ghosts, and Twilight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-24T16:27:08-07:00","id":1238409,"title":"Changeling 2e, Hedge ghosts, and Twilight","content":"This has been on my mind since the backer previews, but I've neglected to bring it up until now, since now is the errata phase during which actual content is revised. At the same time, it's a subjective point and not a clear error, so the errata thread does not seem appropriate for it. I'm posting here with the hope that it might be noticed and considered before the final version of the book. It's also not really something that breaks Changeling 2e, which is overall a quite good game and a fine successor to an excellent forebear. But it still itches at my mind.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why Hedge ghosts have a special form of dematerialization that is explicitly not the Twilight state. I do understand that they spend most of their time in the Hedge for which they are named, which has no natural Twilight state, and that the book is able to save a whole lot of words by making the system of Manifestations and Influence Conditions used by other ephemeral entities. But that leaves us with this:<ul><li>We have Hedge ghosts, who can (temporarily and under harsh penalties) enter the mortal world. They enter in a dematerialized state that's invisible and incorporeal, even to other incorporeal beings, but which is explicitly not Twilight. They can temporarily materialize at a Glamour cost around the focus of one of their Influences, a rough thematic approximation of how Twilit spirits manifest.</li> <li>We also have the Helldiver kith, with its unique ability to dive into a similar invisible, incorporeal form that is not Twilit. This form acts <i>&quot;like a dematerialized Hedge ghost (p. 249), unable to physically interact with anything except other immaterial beings or objects, such as Hedge ghosts, other Helldivers, changelings using the Whispers of Morning Contract (p. 143), the unquiet dead, and spirits of all stripes.&quot;</i> This is not how dematerialized Hedge ghosts are stated to act, which is a little confusing, but maybe Helldivers just work differently in this way and it's just awkwardly worded.</li> <li>Finally, we have the aforementioned Whispers of Morning, which renders a changeling invisible and incorporeal, but able to see and physically interact with <i>&quot;other incorporeal fae creatures and objects, such as other changelings using Whispers of Morning and Hedge ghosts.&quot;</i> She cannot see or interact with spirits or original-flavor ghosts, because <i>&quot;she exists on a different frequency than creatures in Twilight.&quot;</i> This bothers me the most, because the distinction between this being a new, separate phase of Twilight, and being its own state of fae incorporeality that isn't Twilight, is effectively meaningless except that the latter needs to be explained in more words. Creatures in Twilight already exist at different &quot;frequencies&quot; to one another in this way, even using that same word at times. All beings in Twilight don't share one &quot;frequency.&quot;</li> </ul><b>The issue summarized:</b> The book describes behavior that aligns fairly neatly with how Twilight has been described in different gamelines, but spends words and a sidebar specifying that it is not a Twilit state, without clarifying a clear difference.<br /> <br /> <b>The proposal:</b> I think the book would read more naturally to simply state that there is another &quot;phase&quot; of Twilight separate from that of ghosts or spirits, a fae Twilight. Incorporeal Hedge ghosts and changelings using Whispers of Morning would share this phase and be able to see and interact with one another, but not ghosts or spirits, as Twilight phases normally work. In turn, ghosts and spirits would not be able to see or interact with beings in fae Twilight. I assume a Helldiver using her kith ability would exist in a special Twilight state as a property of that power, able to see and interact with all phases of Twilight, so that Helldivers could still interact with Twilit spirits or enter ephemeral irises into the Underworld, because that's the Helldiver's thing. There are already some other individual powers in other games that do this; they're also exception cases.<br /> <br /> <b>Does it matter?:</b> Not much; the practical result is largely the same. But it would be cleaner and consistent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unrelated random comments about Changeling 2e:</b> Ethan Skemp's two-page foreword is beautiful, as is the design of the page backgrounds used by the foreword and certain other pages, like the Character Creation Quick Reference. It Happened to Me jumps around between episodes in a way I find hard to follow, but Wendy's experience with the children is very moving and resonant. It still feels awkward to me that Ogres favor the Shield and not the Sword Regalia, which contains more of the effects that feel traditionally Ogrish, even with the Ogre's renewed focus on harnessing their strength to protect what's dear to them. Ultimately, that these are the complaints that stick with me says more good than bad about how Changeling 2e turned out. Good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T19:16:07-07:00","id":1238476,"title":"","content":"I'd mention it in the errata thread, and I agree: Twilight should remain the catchall term for such ephemeral entities; not only ghosts and spirits exist in Twilight, but so do God-Machine Angels and Goetia. The only entities so far that are <s>ephemeral</s> <i>insubstantial</i> but don't normally exist in Twilight are the Strix, and they have different rules than the others.<br /> <br /> Also, from page 124 of the core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless they Manifest or use a power to appear, ephemeral<br /> beings remain in their insubstantial state when in the material<br /> world. This state is described as \u201cTwilight.\u201d </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-24-2018, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T19:54:50-07:00","id":1238485,"title":"","content":"Ephemera is a defined substance within the setting, and not just the term for anything that naturally exists in Twilight. For example, Quashmallim are not ephemeral despite being in Twilight.<br /> But that just makes Hedge Ghosts make even less sense! Even if the devs for whatever reason wish to make hedge ghosts non-ephemeral (a reason I'd very much like explained as it's far from obvious reading the book) why not still use Twilight for them? It already has a precedent and makes the setting feel more cohesive, imo.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also, Strix aren't ephemeral.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T20:17:50-07:00","id":1238489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1238409-changeling-2e-hedge-ghosts-and-twilight?p=1238485#post1238485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also, Strix aren't ephemeral.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I meant insubstantial but was thinking about &quot;ephemeral entities&quot; when I typed it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T03:47:19-07:00","id":1238543,"title":"","content":"One issue with this: unlike every other ChroD core book published to date, Changeling doesn't give rules for Ephemeral Entities or Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T04:59:23-07:00","id":1238557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1238409-changeling-2e-hedge-ghosts-and-twilight?p=1238543#post1238543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue with this: unlike every other ChroD core book published to date, Changeling doesn't give rules for Ephemeral Entities or Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eeehhm... Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T05:32:39-07:00","id":1238561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1238409-changeling-2e-hedge-ghosts-and-twilight?p=1238543#post1238543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue with this: unlike every other ChroD core book published to date, Changeling doesn't give rules for Ephemeral Entities or Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't that they don't reuse the same rules. No, switching it up to better fit the game is a good thing. The problem is that it's specifically not Twilight and that word count is spent on explaining that fact when it'd take at most the same word count saying that they're separate from ghosts and spirits, and definitely less word count not bringing it up at all.<br /> So we get a very deliberate design choice specifying that A does not have the previously established quality X because it instead has the new quality Y that is mechanically identical (except possibly less interaction with the shared setting) with this design choice having no explanation or apparent reason.<br /> I'm much more interested in hearing why this is than I am changing the book. Are they deliberately separating hedge ghosts from the other gamelines by disallowing cross-Twilight effects (despite half of such effects I know of still would include hedge ghosts)? What is the intent? How does this choice enhance this game?<br /> <br /> Edit: My enthusiasm about this topic should not be confused with anger. I'm a little frustrated, but not more than over any other mystery I have no solution to. I'm just a very curious person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-25-2018, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}